# Entry Main. `node\c` written inside `Add\add` addresses Add, the Structure the body belongs to: with `c` declared
# in Add the write lands in `Add\c` (1), and the root place `c` of the file is another place (0). A `node\c` with no
# `c` in Add is refused with 3 -- an ordinary refusal of a reached place (the pair control of the row
# struct_body_caller_place_write).
# Norm: the book #call-frame (node and its explicit lexical access belong to the actually selected occurrence).
int: c 0
Add:
    int: c 0
    add:
        node\c := 1
    end: add
end: Add
Main:
    Add\add()
